==Plot summary==
During the [[Battle of Eriadu]], [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Gavi Takitaken]] finally begins to feel that [[the Force]] is with him. As he and his allies continue to fight the [[Nihil]] invaders, he joins [[Emelsine Tarkin]], [[Svi'no Atchapat]], and [[Alys Ongwa|Alys "Crash" Ongwa]] to protect civilians. Meanwhile, [[Ruu]] continues to defend against the Nihil. As Takitaken brings civilians to cover, he thinks about finally overcoming his fear and joining the Force. He thinks of his friends in turn, scattered across [[the galaxy]] in the woven threads through which he perceives the Force. To his surprise, however, he senses the presence of his former best friend, [[Driggit Parse]], who had betrayed him and joined the Nihil. 

Driggit Parse looks out over the battle from the [[Bridge (starship)|bridge]] of the ''[[Star Hopper]]''. She is assured of her imminent [[death]]. She reflects upon her actions which led her to this moment, wherein the Nihil [[commander]] known as [[the Warden]] yells at and abuses his subordinates. She is intent on getting her revenge against the Nihil. Parse convinces the Warden to let her mobilize his fleet of [[drill ship]]s. The Warden takes the opportunity to compliment her on her drive, which he sees as akin to his own. Even so, he makes it clear that she will always be beneath him. 

Back on the battlefield, Takitaken is determined to find Parse. He explains to Ruu and Ongwa their connection forged throughout their shared childhood. Now, he senses her fear, and he refuses to leave her behind again. Ruu volunteers to join Takitaken to find Parse. Emelsine Tarkin wants to join as well, but Ongwa impresses upon her the need to be a leader  for the people. Even so, Tarkin reveals that Parse has been working as a [[spy]] for her and the [[Eriaduan resistance]].

Driggit Parse goes to [[the Warden's stronghold]] in [[Eriadu City]], where his fleet of drill ships lies. She rushes the [[pilot]]s to board the reverse-engineered craft. She arrives at the point of no return. With the Warden's permission, she launches the drill ships. She quickly goes to her bag and pulls out a [[Bomb|detonator]], exploding the [[Unidentified Nihil (The Warden's stronghold)|Nihil]] in the control room. 

Gavi Takitaken sees a series of smokestacks rising from the Warden's stronghold. Indeed, Parse deploys more and more detonators, destroying the Nihil forces within. Outside the stronghold, Takitaken senses Parse nearby, but also senses a change in her demeanor. He realizes that she is blowing up the stronghold despite still being inside. Parse is no longer afraid, believing she has cut every tie that binds her. Conversely, Takitaken recognizes his fear but knows the Force is with him. 

Parse's and Takitaken's worlds collide as Parse bursts out of the stronghold as Takitaken starts to enter it. Parse is shocked to see her friend, but [[Blaster|blasts]] a Nihil sneaking up from behind the Padawan. As Parse's charges detonate, Takitaken saves her by [[Telekinesis|pulling]] her with the Force away from the blast. Parse is upset to find that Takitaken is on Eriadu where he faces danger. The Padawan, however, is intent on talking to his friend and helping her. She does not believe she is worth it. Takitaken embraces Parse in forgiveness, bringing her to tears and melting her heart. The pair are soon confronted by a piece of debris falling straight down at them. They are saved by Ruu, who slices through the debris with his [[lightsaber]]. 

Crash Ongwa and her allies are terrified to see [[Spiral-class Viz-Core Eviscerator|Eviscerators]] in the skies, knowing the illegal ships could destroy all of [[Eriadu City]]. Takitaken fears the battle has been lost, but Parse pulls out a device which overrides the cooling systems of the Eviscerators, causing them all to overheat and explode. This infuriates the Warden. He calls Parse, and she announces her sabotage and betrayal. With the Warden's fury growing, Parse destroyed her [[comlink]]. 

Ruu, Parse, and Takitaken work together to fight thre Nihil. Takitaken is eager to finally go back to [[Valo]] with his best friend. Before they can continue their conversation, the Nihil attack a civilian family. Ruu and Takitaken use the Force to shield the family with pieces of rubble as Parse fights off the Nihil. She takes her friend's lightsaber and battles the Nihil. Meanwhile, she thinks of her past and her hopes for the future. In the aftermath, she informs Takitaken that she cannot go back to Valo after the things she has done; she would not be accepted. 

Driggit Parse pulls out a [[thermal detonator]], apologizing to Takitaken. She chucks it in the air before it explodes. After Takitaken regains his senses, he finds his lightsaber on the ground and Parse nowhere to be seen. Despite wanting to go after his friend, he knows his duty is to protect the [[Eriaduan]]s. Further, he can feel her in the Force. He is comforted knowing their bond is healing, even if it is not fully fixed. 

